---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import communitiesData from '@data/communities.json';
import { SOCIALS } from '../config';
import '@styles/practice.css';

const linkedin = SOCIALS.find((social) => social.label === 'LinkedIn')!;

---

<Layout
  title="About | Karan Mittal"
  description="Karan Mittal is an independent engineer building graph-grounded knowledge systems and LLM evaluations, co-founder of Dextar, and a community organiser in Indore."
>
  <main class="practice-page about-page">
    <section class="about-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div class="about-hero-copy">
        <span class="register">About</span>
        <h1 id="about-title">An engineer-scientist, invested in the outcome.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          I like understanding difficult problems and building stable systems that actually solve
          them. The work matters when it makes an organisation more effective and leaves people
          with something they can rely on.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="about-portrait">
        <div class="portrait-frame">
          <img
            src="/profile.jpg"
            srcset="/profile-400.jpg 400w, /profile.jpg 800w"
            sizes="(max-width: 880px) 100vw, 440px"
            alt="Karan Mittal speaking at a technical event"
            width="800"
            height="800"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          Leading a hands-on systems workshop on agent architectures and retrieval boundaries.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 01: Working Method (Stepped Vertical Narrative with Accent Spine) -->
    <section class="section about-method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="section-intro method-intro">
        <span class="register">Working method</span>
        <h2 id="method-title">The problem comes before the tool.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          I work independently with teams building knowledge systems: graph-grounded retrieval,
          LLM evaluation, and the data infrastructure beneath them. I also co-founded
          <a href="https://dextar.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dextar</a>, and my research
          is in graph theory. The work has taken me through enterprise knowledge platforms,
          semiconductor supply chain traceability, and biomedical data.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="method-spine-wrap">
        <ol class="method-spine-steps">
          <li class="method-spine-step">
            <div class="step-spine-indicator">
              <span class="step-spine-pin">01</span>
            </div>
            <div class="step-spine-content">
              <h3>Understand the operating reality.</h3>
              <p>Start with the people, the workflow, and the constraints before selecting an implementation.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="method-spine-step">
            <div class="step-spine-indicator">
              <span class="step-spine-pin">02</span>
            </div>
            <div class="step-spine-content">
              <h3>Build from evidence.</h3>
              <p>Investigate what is happening, test possible explanations, and make the system’s boundaries inspectable.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="method-spine-step">
            <div class="step-spine-indicator">
              <span class="step-spine-pin">03</span>
            </div>
            <div class="step-spine-content">
              <h3>Leave the team with ownership.</h3>
              <p>The team should understand what was built, why it works that way, and how to operate and improve it.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="actions method-actions">
        <a href="/publications/" class="more-link">Writing and talks</a>
        <a href="/now/" class="more-link">What I’m working on now</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section: Personal Intellectual History -->
    <section class="section about-history" aria-labelledby="history-title">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <span class="register">Background</span>
        <h2 id="history-title">From distributed storage to inspectable graphs.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          My perspective is shaped by engineering at the boundary between low-level infrastructure and high-consequence decision systems.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="history-narrative">
        <p>
          I started in systems engineering with distributed storage, Linux internals, and
          data-intensive pipelines. Distributed consensus and transactional integrity made one
          principle clear: complex systems rarely fail inside isolated algorithms. They fail at the
          unverified boundaries between subsystems, in the gap between assumed state and
          operational reality. When machine learning moved into production, that same failure mode
          amplified — teams treated probabilistic model output as an oracle rather than as an
          unverified component.
        </p>
        <p>
          My work since has been grounding those decisions in explicit graph structures: material
          lots, chemical regulations, and supplier claims captured as inspectable records where
          uncertainty carries an explicit operational cost. At <a href="https://dextar.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dextar</a> and in independent
          advisory the goal is unchanged — systems whose boundaries can be inspected, whose state
          can be audited, and that engineering teams can own and operate with confidence.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 02: Community & Teaching (Dense Single-Line Ledger) -->
    <section class="section community-section" id="community" aria-labelledby="community-title">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <span class="register">Community and teaching</span>
          <h2 id="community-title">Helping people build is part of the work.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="community-head-actions">
          <a class="more-link" href="/publications/#talks">Talks and workshops</a>
          <a class="more-link" href={linkedin.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="community-lead">
        I organise, speak, and mentor in technical communities across Central India. Workshops
        and conversations are a practical way to share what I understand and learn from others.
      </p>

      <div class="community-ledger">
        {communitiesData.communities.map((community) => (
          <article class="community-ledger-row">
            <div class="community-main">
              <h3>{community.name}</h3>
              <p>{community.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="community-links">
              {community.links.map((link) => (
                <a href={link.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="community-link">
                  <span>{link.label}</span>
                </a>
              ))}
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 03: Closing CTA -->
    <section class="section closing" aria-labelledby="about-closing-title">
      <span class="register">Work together</span>
      <h2 id="about-closing-title">Bring a problem worth solving.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        I work with teams whose knowledge systems have to be trusted: answers that trace back to
        evidence, evaluations that catch regressions, and graphs that stay correct as the data
        changes.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a href="/contact/" class="button">Discuss your problem</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ================================================================
     1. Hero: Asymmetric Wider Portrait Split
     ================================================================ */
  .about-hero {
    display: grid;
    min-height: auto;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(300px, 400px);
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6.5rem) 0;
  }

  .about-hero-copy .lead {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .about-portrait {
    width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .portrait-frame {
    border-radius: 18px;
    corner-shape: squircle;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .portrait-frame img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 28%;
    filter: saturate(0.92) contrast(1.02);
  }

  .about-portrait figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ie-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--ie-type-ui);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     2. Working Method: Stepped Vertical Narrative with Accent Spine
     ================================================================ */
  .about-method {
    padding-top: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem);
  }

  .method-intro {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .method-intro p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .method-spine-wrap {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .method-spine-steps {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .method-spine-step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.75rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .step-spine-indicator {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .step-spine-pin {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 2.25rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    color: var(--ie-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--ie-type-small);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .step-spine-content {
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .step-spine-content h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: var(--ie-type-h3);
    color: var(--ie-ink);
  }

  .step-spine-content p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ie-ink-secondary);
    font-size: var(--ie-type-base);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .method-actions {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .history-narrative {
    max-width: 72ch;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .history-narrative p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ie-ink-secondary);
    font-size: var(--ie-type-h4);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* ================================================================
     3. Community: Dense Single-Line Ledger
     ================================================================ */
  .community-head-actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .community-lead {
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--ie-ink-secondary);
    font-size: var(--ie-type-h4);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .community-ledger {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ie-rule);
  }

  .community-ledger-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ie-rule);
    transition: background-color 140ms ease;
  }

  .community-main h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    font-size: var(--ie-type-h4);
    color: var(--ie-ink);
  }

  .community-main p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ie-ink-secondary);
    font-size: var(--ie-type-small);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .community-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .community-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 44px;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--ie-type-ui);
    color: var(--ie-blue);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .community-link::after {
    content: '\2197';
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }

  .community-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
  }

  /* Responsive Adjustments */
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .about-hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2.5rem;
      padding-block: 3.5rem 3rem;
    }

    .about-portrait {
      max-width: 320px;
    }

    .community-ledger-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.35rem;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .community-ledger-row {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
